<title>BRAZIL: Brazil to issue 10-year 150-200 mln stg bond.</title>
<headline>Brazil to issue 10-year 150-200 mln stg bond.</headline>
<dateline>BRASILIA 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil plans to issue a 150-200 million stg, 10-year Eurobond via Barclays de Zoete Wedd and CS First Boston in early July, the Central Bank said.</p>
<p>In a statement, the bank also said it would not issue a Euroyen bond for the time being.</p>
<p>The bank said it had received recommendations from Japanese financial institutions regarding the possibility of issuing a Euroyen bond, but the bank decided to &quot;wait for a more opportune moment to enter this market.&quot;</p>
</text>
